---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '@/components/PageHero.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '@/components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { POLICY_LAST_UPDATED, SITE } from '@/lib/site';

const updated = new Date(`${POLICY_LAST_UPDATED}T00:00:00Z`).toLocaleDateString('en-GB', { day: 'numeric', month: 'long', year: 'numeric', timeZone: 'UTC' });
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How NeoKemetAI handles information: what is collected when you visit, contact-form messages, YouTube embeds, cookies and third-party links."
>
  <PageHero kicker="Privacy" title="Privacy policy" glyph="𓂀">
    <Breadcrumbs slot="above" items={[{ label: 'Privacy', href: '/privacy/' }]} />
  </PageHero>

  <div class="container section prose policy">
    <div class="updated">Last updated: <time datetime={POLICY_LAST_UPDATED}>{updated}</time></div>

    <p>
      {SITE.name} is an educational website about ancient Egypt. We aim to collect as little information about visitors as
      possible. This policy explains what information is involved when you use the site, and why.
    </p>

    <h2>Visiting the site</h2>
    <p>
      You can read every page without creating an account or giving us any personal information. The site is served as
      static pages by our hosting provider, Vercel. Like any web server, its infrastructure receives technical information
      needed to deliver pages and protect the service, such as your IP address, browser type, the page requested and the time
      of the request. This information is handled by Vercel under its own privacy policy and is kept in short-lived server
      logs; we do not use it to identify visitors.
    </p>

    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      The site does not currently use any analytics, advertising or tracking service. If we add privacy-respecting analytics
      in the future, we will update this policy before doing so.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies and similar technologies</h2>
    <p>
      {SITE.name} does not set cookies and does not use local storage to track you. Fonts are served from our own site, not
      from a third-party font service. Third-party services described below may set their own cookies only when you choose to
      use them.
    </p>

    <h2>YouTube videos</h2>
    <p>
      Pages that feature a NeoKemet film show a preview image loaded from YouTube's image servers (<code>i.ytimg.com</code>),
      which means YouTube receives the standard technical information of that image request. The video player itself is not
      loaded until you click play. It then loads from <code>youtube-nocookie.com</code>, YouTube's privacy-enhanced mode, and
      from that point YouTube (Google) may collect information and set cookies under
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's privacy policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Interactive 3D models</h2>
    <p>
      3D models and their viewer are loaded from this site only when you choose to open them. No third-party service is
      involved.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact form</h2>
    <p>
      When you use the <a href="/contact/">contact form</a>, we receive the name, email address, subject and message you
      enter. The form is processed by a function on our hosting provider (Vercel) and delivered to our inbox by an email
      delivery provider. We use this information only to read and reply to your message; we do not add you to a mailing list,
      sell it or share it for marketing. The form includes simple automatic spam checks that do not involve any third-party
      tracking.
    </p>

    <h2>How long we keep information</h2>
    <p>
      Contact messages are kept in our email for as long as needed to deal with your enquiry and for a reasonable period
      afterwards for reference, then deleted. You can ask us to delete your message at any time. Server logs are kept by our
      hosting provider for a limited period according to its own policy.
    </p>

    <h2>Links to other websites and social media</h2>
    <p>
      Our pages link to museums, archives, academic publications and reference works, and our footer links to NeoKemetAI
      profiles on YouTube, Facebook, TikTok, Instagram and Pinterest. Those links open the other site, which has its own
      privacy practices; we are not responsible for them. Following a social media link does not share any information from
      {SITE.name} with that platform beyond what your browser normally sends when opening a page.
    </p>

    <h2>Third-party services</h2>
    <p>The services involved in running the site are:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Vercel</strong>: hosting and the contact-form function.</li>
      <li><strong>An email delivery provider</strong>: forwarding contact-form messages to our inbox.</li>
      <li><strong>YouTube (Google)</strong>: video preview images, and the player once you press play.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Each processes information under its own privacy policy.</p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>
      {SITE.name} is suitable for learners of all ages but does not knowingly collect personal information from children.
      Children should ask a parent, guardian or teacher before sending us a message.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Depending on where you live, you may have the right to ask what personal information we hold about you, to correct it
      or to have it deleted. Because we hold very little, the only personal information we are likely to have is a message
      you sent us. Contact us and we will help.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this policy when the site changes, for example if we add a new service. The date at the top of the page
      shows when it was last revised.
    </p>

    <h2>Questions</h2>
    <p>For any privacy question or request, please use the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.</p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .updated { color: var(--text-faint); font-size: var(--step--1); margin-bottom: 1.2rem; }
  .policy h2 { margin-top: 2.2rem; }
</style>
